            "review_title": "Review at Tracce Tea And Coffee Shop",
            "review_text": "SoKailua\nOahu58 contributions\n0\nVery cool hidden cafe/lounge in barbed wire bldg\nDec 2017 • Couples\nDon’t know whether or not to post this because I’m pretty sure they do not have many non Vietnamese customers. Their menu is all in Vietnamese and the staff do not speak English, but this place has a sign in English. However, they are so nice we managed to order. I doubt that most tourists will be able to find this place though since it’s in the ba dinh district away from the touristy area. It’s a very short walk from the lotte hotel. The bldg was so run down and had barbed wire, that I had to take a look. You have to go up a flight of stairs. It’s a beautiful 2 level loft with a cafe during the day and bar lounge (with live music) by night. The service was excellent and they serve high quality green tea equivalent to what you can get at a good cafe in Tokyo. I can see Japanese and Korean young women loving this place. Every corner was designed for a perfect Instagram shot. This place is just so cool. At the end of our visit, the hostess gave us markers to sign a wall where all their other customers have signed.\nRead more\nWritten December 6, 2017",
